{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see if payroll verification messages were caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) heard about an email going around asking staff to verify their payroll login and asked if it's real. She hasn't said she received it or clicked anything. Checked: her account is active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Her quarantine has Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain: capital I in place of l in 'brightline'), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-10T20:58Z, flagged phishing and not releasable. It asks users to verify their payroll login, likely a credential harvesting page. She says it's 'going around', so it was probably sent to several users. Still needed: security to review the sender/domain, block it for the whole org, check other mailboxes for delivered copies that weren't quarantined, and send a company-wide warning if appropriate. I've asked the user to tell us right away if she or anyone she knows clicked or entered credentials (that would make it P1 under KB-029).",
  "reason": "KB-008 says to always escalate reported phishing. A lookalike-domain payroll phishing email may be going to several users."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking with us first. That email is not real. It's a phishing scam. Our filters caught a copy sent to you and are holding it, so it never reached your inbox. It comes from an address made to look like ours (\"brightIine\" with a capital I in place of the l). Your payroll is not affected and you don't need to verify anything. If you see a message like this, please don't click links in it, reply to it, or forward it to coworkers. Leave it where it is and report it to us. I've passed this to our security team so they can block the sender for everyone. One important thing: if you or anyone you know clicked a link in it or typed a password, please contact the help desk right away so we can protect the account.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-008. User active, 0 failed logins. Her quarantine has Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-10 20:58 UTC, flagged phishing and not releasable. I did not release anything. User hasn't said she clicked; from what I could check it never reached her inbox. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1) to block the sender org-wide and check other mailboxes, since the user says it's going around. If anyone reports clicking or entering credentials, follow KB-029 (P1).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
